 * @target-api PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}
 *
 * Auth: /api/owners/** is matched by SecurityConfig's "/api/**".authenticated() rule, so a
 * valid JWT (obtained from POST /api/auth/login) is required in the Authorization header.
 * No external HTTP dependency was found by detect-external-calls, so no WireMock stub is used.
 *
 * updateOwner has NO @Valid on the request body, so field-level bean-validation errors are
 * not possible; its only real branches are existsById(ownerId) (-> 404) and owner.setId(ownerId)
 * on a null body (-> NPE -> 500, no @ControllerAdvice present).
